KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.class.spec.match] + [temp.variadic].  A recursive class
template over a NON-type parameter pack (`sum_t<H, T...>` with
`v = H + sum_t<T...>::v`) fails to fold for EXACTLY TWO elements
(`sum_t<2,3>::v` "could not fully type-check ... unsupported construct"), while
0/1/3/4-element sums fold correctly and the TYPE-pack analogue is fine.  The
non-recursive partial-spec deduction is also correct at every arity, so the
defect is specific to the recursive non-type-pack fold at the two-element level
(the `sum_t<T...>` step forwarding a one-element non-type pack).  Residual
surfaced while reproducing the tuple _TupleConstraints shape with a non-type
proxy (the tuple uses TYPE packs -- see cpp11_alias_template_parallel_pack, now
CORE).  Flip to CORE once a recursive non-type-pack fold is correct at two
elements.
